in HIV-1-infected hu-PBL-NOD-SCID mice.</article-title><source>J Exp Med</source><volume>193</volume><fpage>651</fpage><lpage>660</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11238596</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003096-Zhang1"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Pang</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Ding</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Wood</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Identification of a potential HIV-induced source of bystander-mediated apoptosis in T cells: upregulation of trail in primary human macrophages by HIV-1 tat.</article-title><source>J Biomed Sci</source><volume>8</volume><fpage>290</fpage><lpage>296</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11385301</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003096-Badley1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Badley</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><name><surname>McElhinny</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Leibson</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Lynch</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name><name><surname>Alderson</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Upregulation of Fas ligand expression by human immunodeficiency virus in human macrophages mediates apoptosis of uninfected T lymphocytes.</article-title><source>J Virol</source><volume>70</volume><fpage>199</fpage><lpage>206</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8523526</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003096-Badley2"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Badley</surname><given-names>AD</given-names>